Description: SwiftShader linked into the program as ANGLE's Vulkan on Jam OS, its JIT in MAP_JIT memory
 WebGL in software (docs/CR-PLAN.md, CR-e): ANGLE's Vulkan back end on
 SwiftShader, as Linux runs it with --use-angle=swiftshader (or
 swiftshader-webgl, the browser's software WebGL). On Linux ANGLE calls
 Khronos's Vulkan loader, which opens SwiftShader's ICD,
 libvk_swiftshader.so, by its JSON file; Jam OS links programs static and
 has no dlopen, so SwiftShader itself is the program's Vulkan: args.gn
 sets angle_shared_libvulkan and angle_use_custom_libvulkan false (ANGLE
 calls vk* directly, as on macOS, with no mock ICD) and
 angle_vulkan_loader_dir to the group below.
 - build/toolchain/jamos/vulkan: the "libvulkan" group ANGLE links, which
   is SwiftShader's Vulkan source set (its vk* functions are Vulkan's
   entry points), and the three calls of VK_KHR_display the loader
   exports and SwiftShader built for Chromium has not (ANGLE's display
   for a screen without a window system links them), answered as the
   loader answers for a driver without the extension: no displays. New
   files: no layer answers a build's target or a link's symbol.
 - build_overrides/angle.gni: ANGLE's translator links SwiftShader's
   SPIRV-Tools (only its validator, which a release build never calls),
   not Chromium's: SwiftShader brings its own copy, and a static program
   can hold one (two copies' same symbols would mix the two versions, by
   the archives' order). Chromium's own override file: no layer answers.
 - ANGLE's angle_vulkan_icd and ui/gl: no data_deps on the shared
   libvk_swiftshader.so and its ICD file on Jam OS (its link driver refuses
   -shared, and nothing would load them); ANGLE's define of the ICD file's
   name stays, harmless (an environment variable for a loader that isn't
   there). The build's own lines, not a layer's.
 - SwiftShader's Vulkan target: Wayland's headers (Chromium's own
   libwayland's, as its WSI target has them) for its Wayland surface
   code; a Linux build finds them in the sysroot's /usr/include, Jam OS's
   sysroot has none. The build's lines.
 - SwiftShader's Reactor (ExecutableMemory.cpp): its code buffers are
   mapped with MAP_JIT, as on macOS, where Linux maps a memfd so that
   profilers see a name. Jam OS makes only JIT memory executable (private
   anonymous memory mapped with MAP_JIT by a process holding the JIT
   power, section 12), never a file's or a memfd's pages; a layer can't
   tell Reactor's code buffer from any other mapping of a memfd, and
   making every memfd mapping executable would undo the rule. Decommits
   and frees are munmap, as before. Which process may JIT is patch 0914's.
Forwarded: not-needed (Jam OS's: static programs and its W^X rule)
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build/toolchain/jamos/vulkan/BUILD.gn
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Jam OS's Vulkan for ANGLE (ports/chromium in Jam OS, its docs/CR-PLAN.md,
+# CR-e): args.gn's angle_vulkan_loader_dir names this directory, so ANGLE's
+# Vulkan back end (with angle_shared_libvulkan and angle_use_custom_libvulkan
+# false) links this "libvulkan" in place of Khronos's loader. Jam OS runs
+# static programs and has no dlopen, so no loader could open an ICD: the one
+# Vulkan driver is SwiftShader's, linked into the program, whose vk*
+# functions are Vulkan's own entry points (it is a whole libvulkan, as
+# libvk_swiftshader.so is when a program opens it by name).
+group("libvulkan") {
+  deps = [
+    ":display",
+    "//third_party/swiftshader/src/Vulkan:_swiftshader_libvulkan",
+  ]
+}
+
+# What the loader exports and SwiftShader has not: VK_KHR_display's calls,
+# which ANGLE's display for a screen without a window system links (and
+# uses only when asked for that display). They answer as the loader does
+# for a driver without the extension: no displays.
+source_set("display") {
+  sources = [ "display.cc" ]
+  deps = [ "//third_party/vulkan-headers/src:vulkan_headers" ]
+}
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build/toolchain/jamos/vulkan/display.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+// Jam OS's Vulkan for ANGLE (BUILD.gn here): VK_KHR_display's calls, which
+// SwiftShader built for Chromium leaves out (its display surfaces are
+// Linux's KMS), answered as Khronos's loader answers them for a driver
+// without the extension: no displays, and no display surface.
+
+#include <vulkan/vulkan.h>
+
+extern "C" {
+
+VKAPI_ATTR VkResult VKAPI_CALL
+vkGetPhysicalDeviceDisplayPropertiesKHR(VkPhysicalDevice physical_device,
+                                        uint32_t* count,
+                                        VkDisplayPropertiesKHR* properties) {
+  *count = 0;
+  return VK_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+VKAPI_ATTR VkResult VKAPI_CALL
+vkGetDisplayModePropertiesKHR(VkPhysicalDevice physical_device,
+                              VkDisplayKHR display,
+                              uint32_t* count,
+                              VkDisplayModePropertiesKHR* properties) {
+  *count = 0;
+  return VK_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+VKAPI_ATTR VkResult VKAPI_CALL
+vkCreateDisplayPlaneSurfaceKHR(VkInstance instance,
+                               const VkDisplaySurfaceCreateInfoKHR* info,
+                               const VkAllocationCallbacks* allocator,
+                               VkSurfaceKHR* surface) {
+  return VK_ERROR_EXTENSION_NOT_PRESENT;
+}
+
+}  // extern "C"
